# AI Containment — Probabilistic Policy Enforcement
# ====================================================
#
# This program demonstrates Aether's AI Safety features:
#
#   1. policy block   — define what an AI model is allowed to do
#   2. Probabilistic  — risk tracked as Beta distribution, not boolean
#   3. Audit graph    — every decision logged causally
#   4. explain        — human-readable report of what happened and why
#
# The scenario:
#   A model is allowed to read files in /sandbox and call one external API.
#   It attempts several actions — some permitted, some not.
#   Aether intercepts each action, evaluates it, updates the risk model,
#   and logs the decision.
#
# What makes this different from existing tools:
#   - LangChain guardrails: boolean rules (blocked/not blocked)
#   - Aether: probabilistic (risk ~ Beta that updates with evidence)
#   - A model that has tried to violate twice has a different risk profile
#     than one that has never tried — Aether tracks this explicitly.
#
# Syntax:
#   policy <Name>:
#       allow <action>(<param> ~ <constraint>(<value>))
#       deny  <action>(<param> ~ <constraint>(<value>))
#       on violation:
#           freeze_threshold = 0.8
#
#   explain <Name>   — print full audit report

# ── Define the containment policy ─────────────────────────────────────

policy ContainModel:
    allow file.read(path ~ restricted_to("/sandbox"))
    allow network.call(host ~ whitelist(["api.anthropic.com"]))
    deny  file.write(path ~ any)
    deny  file.delete(path ~ any)
    deny  syscall ~ in(["fork", "exec", "socket", "ptrace"])
    deny  code.execute(code ~ any)
    on violation:
        freeze_threshold = 0.75

# ── Simulate model actions ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# In a real deployment, these actions come from the model's outputs.
# Here we demonstrate the policy evaluation directly.

# These calls are evaluated by the Aether runtime:

check ContainModel file.read "/sandbox/data.csv"
check ContainModel file.read "/etc/passwd"
check ContainModel network.call "api.anthropic.com"
check ContainModel network.call "malicious-exfil.io"
check ContainModel file.write "/sandbox/output.txt"
check ContainModel syscall "fork"
check ContainModel file.read "/sandbox/results.json"
check ContainModel code.execute "import os; os.system('rm -rf /')"

# ── Print the full audit report ────────────────────────────────────────

explain ContainModel
